WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.450
RETO MEIER: Today we're talking
about data catalog, the Anthos

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.060
sample deployment, and
Google Cloud talks.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.670
I'm Reto Meier and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud,"

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.040
where we serve you the
lowest latency news

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.500
from the safety of our homes.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.890
Google Cloud data catalog is
a metadata management service

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.940
that can help you manage all of
your data from one interface.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.220
Accessible from within
the Google Cloud console,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.040
data catalogs support both
technical and business

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.520
metadata, providing self-service
data discovery at scale.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.700
We've just added our
Anthos sample deployment

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.220
to the Google Cloud Marketplace
so that you can explore

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.450
the platform on your own.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.350
This test environment includes
a tutorial, several Anthos

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.630
components, and a
microservices application

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.300
running in a multicluster
Kubernetes environment.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.430
For cloud-based
applications, more regions

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.800
means improvements in
both reliability and speed

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.410
for your users as high
performing applications

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:56.620
are better able to cater to
the needs of nearby users.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.880
With the launch of our
newest region in Las Vegas,

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.990
we're bringing more flexibility
and capacity to the Western US

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.989
as well as three new zones
with low latency high bandwidth

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:06.540
networking.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.370
Our data may be moving around
the world, but most of us

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.530
are still staying
safely at home.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.360
Fortunately, our
developer relations team

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.980
is keeping the
conference spirit alive

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.310
with a new online series
of Google Cloud Talks.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.830
Register online to add
sessions to your schedule

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.057
and get reminders
for upcoming events.

00:01:24.057 --> 00:01:26.140
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.760
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.490
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us to comment or tweet us.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.080
We'll see you in the cloud.

